@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`Flask.run` currently treats the first colon in `SERVER_NAME` as the host-port
+separator. See proposal.md for motivation.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+
+- Recognize the brackets around an IPv6 address before separating its optional
+  port.
+- Leave existing hostname parsing and the explicit port-zero condition intact.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+
+- Change URL routing or general `SERVER_NAME` validation.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Use a small bracket-aware branch in the existing default-selection logic.
+  It keeps this behavior local to `run` and preserves the current handling for
+  ordinary hostnames. A general URL parser is unnecessary because this code
+  only needs the configured host and optional port.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Malformed bracketed values retain the existing conversion-error behavior for
+  invalid ports. → Limit the change to valid bracketed IPv6 host-and-port input.
