@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+`SERVER_NAME` supports documented host-and-port values, but the development
+server defaults misparse bracketed IPv6 literals and cannot bind to the
+configured address.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Parse a bracketed IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` with an optional port correctly when
+  selecting `Flask.run` defaults.
+- Preserve existing hostname and port-zero default behavior.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `development-server-defaults`: Development-server host and port defaults
+  derived from application configuration.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- None. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/flask/app.py` run-default parsing.
+- `tests/test_basic.py` coverage for IPv6 configuration defaults.
